      "html": "<ul><li>There are two main regimes: LOLER 1998 for lifting equipment and PSSR 2000 for pressure systems.</li><li>Both examinations are duties, done by a competent person.</li><li>A defect that is a danger to people must be reported promptly. Serious cases can mean telling the enforcing authority.</li><li>The written scheme sets what is examined, how and when. The report ties back to it.</li><li>Photos and severity recorded on the spot beat notes written later.</li><li>Quickler records the examination and writes the report. It does not certify the plant. You do.</li></ul>"
