      "heading": "What engineering insurance inspection is for",
      "html": "<p>An insurer's engineer surveyor does statutory examinations of a client's plant. Most often that is lifting equipment and pressure systems. It protects people, meets the client's legal duties, and shows the insurer the real risk.</p><p>Software does not do the examination. You do. It helps you record it on site and turn it into the report.</p>"
