      "html": "<p>The Lifting Operations and Lifting Equipment Regulations 1998 need lifting equipment to get a thorough examination by a competent person. Often that is every six months for equipment that lifts people or an accessory, and every twelve months for other lifting equipment, or under an examination scheme. It covers cranes, hoists, lifts, slings and chains.</p><p>Quickler records each item, its result and any defect, with how serious it is and a photo. Then it writes the report. It does not make equipment safe. Check the current LOLER requirements.</p>"
