      "html": "<p>The Pressure Systems Safety Regulations 2000 need some pressure systems to have a written scheme of examination. That includes boilers, steam plant, air receivers and compressors. A competent person draws it up. The system must be examined to it before the due date. You look for corrosion, cracking and wastage.</p><p>Quickler ties the examination to the scheme and its due dates, records your findings with photos, and writes the report. It does not draw up the scheme or say the system is safe to run. Check the current PSSR requirements.</p>"
